4. V6-m12: F-4b, EVERY SOURCE AT ITS BOUND AT ONCE (44.1338 A): a ribbon conductor 1.00418 A at -20 C against its printed 1 A (with a fourth lead 0.7884 A)
   DECISION (authority: SESSION; authority_why: a fault-set definition inside engineering, no requirement, money or claim changes;
   ruled_by: Slot A under the owner's standing rule of 26 September 2026; ruled_on: 5 October 2026; reversed_by: none): the design need
   not serve F-4b inside the ribbons' printed rating. Reason: F-4b is five independent overloads at once (four stage current limits and
   U601's), outside the single-failure set the architecture's failure table names (ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA section 12: every row one failure);
   each single overload (F-4a) holds; the excess is 0.42 % at the cold end at the extreme contact vertex only. Reverse: carry the fourth
   return lead (0.7884 A there).

5. V6-m8: THE XT60 ROWS. Neither held XT60 sheet (V1.2: 30 A, no condition; 2021V1: 35 A with 12 AWG, rise under 85 C) names a
   board-soldered end: none is named. The rows' largest XT60 contact current 11.0311 A is judged against the printed 30 A as the WIRE-TO-WIRE rating, a
   63 % margin; the board-soldered end's rating is MISSING (vendor task, UNSENT: Amass, the XT60-F's rating soldered into a board, its
   land and the board's copper), PROVISIONAL with that margin

